  <uml:Package xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499761463063_699735_22045" xmi:uuid="d318e308-b08f-4cd8-b6ec-a2af312a09b5" xmi:type="uml:Package">
    <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_4_1_8e001ed_1510151217504_470058_31132" xmi:uuid="0579ed19-b62a-4acd-9cda-ea44d9650f53" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
      <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499761463063_699735_22045"/>
      <body>This capability provides the ability to represent geometric models describing the shape of a part. Geometric structures and transformations are supported by describing the relationships between geometric models. The Figure &lt;caption&gt;Relating geometric models by a placement transformation&lt;/caption&gt;, Figure &lt;caption&gt;Relating geometric models by a cartesian transformation&lt;/caption&gt; and Figure &lt;caption&gt;Relating geometric models without a transformation&lt;/caption&gt; illustrate the different ways, how two geometric models can be related: by a placement transformation, by a cartesian transformation, or without a transformation. &lt;note&gt;The transformation matrices exchanged using this Domain model are not guaranteed to be orthogonal. Therefore in the case of multi-level assembly the concatenation of the transformation matrices may result in inconsistent or incorrect results between exchange partners.&lt;/note&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;PlacementTransformation.png&lt;/name&gt;Relating geometric models by a placement transformation&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;CartesianTransformation.png&lt;/name&gt;Relating geometric models by a cartesian transformation&lt;/figure&gt; &lt;figure&gt;&lt;name&gt;SameCoordinateSpace.png&lt;/name&gt;Relating geometric models without a transformation&lt;/figure&gt; This capability represents the information necessary to transform elements from different geometric coordinate spaces and coordinate systems.</body>
    </ownedComment>
