    <packagedElement xmi:id="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193074_744764_23521" xmi:uuid="956354fd-0cfc-414c-818e-64d409ce5ac0" xmi:type="uml:Class">
      <ownedComment xmi:id="_18_0_5_45e01bd_1456303092486_377957_42994" xmi:uuid="01066208-2e68-46cf-a43e-f2c70c220212" xmi:type="uml:Comment">
        <annotatedElement xmi:idref="_18_4_1_e120334_1499417193074_744764_23521"/>
        <body>A Direction is a type of DetailedGeometricModelItem. A Direction is an object that defines a general direction vector in two or three-dimensional space. The actual magnitudes of the components have no effect upon the direction being defined, only the ratios x:y:z or x:y are significant. &lt;note&gt;The components of this entity are not normalised. If a unit vector is required, it should be normalised before use.&lt;/note&gt;</body>
      </ownedComment>
      <name>Direction</name>
      <generalization xmi:id="_18_4_1_8db01ea_1533199760483_933135_97596" xmi:uuid="98b9fd3f-25fc-46b6-b9bf-7f94224e7fda" xmi:type="uml:Generalization">
